ity-sensitive-fix-scope false --fix-replay-required-rows 0 --fix-replay-passing-rows 0. Record its decision, stopReason and blockedBy in an event line of your state log. When the decision is STOP, synthesize and end with that stopReason; otherwise continue, aiming the next iteration at what blockedBy or the graph trace names.\n9: \n10: Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only. Underscore emphasis around a command name is not dropped, because a command name may hold an underscore. The two moved baseline rows are judged without their text: 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/lead-diag.mjs prints only lead indices. The open P2 list in 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md and the open P2 of review passes ten to thirteen (review-report-pass-10.md, review-report-pass-11.md, review-report-pass-12.md, review-report.md) are already recorded. The holdout gate is read by its count only, never its rows. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code; it writes only inside its lineage folder and through the two scripts above."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor