{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794868738931,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e683785d001Zi6p2zr6g1jOzz","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e6834a2f001LvS67tJZvKNpKs","type":"tool","id":"call_161252a3c6ee41849ec1e9e7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"do not run it\\|declined\\|pronoun\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --include=\"*.md\" | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md:131:No task was marked `[B]`. Three follow-ups were declined, each on its task line: a rate-text assertion in T007, a refusal of one arm named twice in T018 and a shared-fixture extraction in T022.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:85:- [x] T007 [P] Print a range beside the followed rate and the load rate (`$CTS`, then `$S` functions `wilsonRange` and `tallyBlock`). Edit the functions in the order named, one at a time, and run the named test after each. Test first: add a `describe('wilsonRange')` block with the cases `wilsonRange(8, 16)` equals `{ low: 0.28, high: 0.72 }`, `wilsonRange(0, 16)` equals `{ low: 0, high: 0.19 }`, `wilsonRange(16, 16)` equals `{ low: 0.81, high: 1 }` and `wilsonRange(0, 0)` is `null`, and in `describe('run log summary')` add the case `prints a range beside each workflow rate`, which asserts the `workflow` block holds `followedRange` and `loadRange` equal to `wilsonRange` of each rate's two counts. They fail because `wilsonRange` is not exported. Then export `wilsonRange(successes, total)`, the Wilson score interval at 1.96 rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, and add the two fields to the `workflow` object in `tallyBlock`. `followedRate`, `loadRate` and `share` keep their text. Verify: `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports the new cases failed before the change and 0 failed after it. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run wilsonRange is not a function (5 failed), then 144 passed of 144. Typecheck exit 0. Optional rate-text assertion declined: the rate text and the range come from the same counts\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:88:- [x] T018 Refuse a pair the summary cannot use (`$CTS`, then `$S` function `selectMode`). After T009. This task changes the function `selectMode` and nothing else. Test first: add the case `refuses a pair without a summary or with one arm name`, which expects `runScorer(['--runtime', 'claude', '--locator', '{}', '--pair', 'pre,post'])` to exit with a status other than 0 and an error output that holds `--pair needs --summary`, and expects `runScorer(['--summary', 'missing-log.jsonl', '--pair', 'pre'])` to exit with a status other than 0 and an error output that holds `--pair needs two arm names`. It fails because neither message exists. Then in `selectMode`, inside the `if (options.summaryLogs !== null)` block before `return 'summary';`, throw `new UsageError('--pair needs two arm names, as <from>,<to>')` when `options.pair` is a string that does not split on `,` into exactly two non-empty names. After that block, before the `--runtime` check, throw `new UsageError('--pair needs --summary')` when `options.pair` is not `null`. Verify: the file reports the new case failed before the change and 0 failed after it. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run missing --pair needs --summary (1 failed), then 147 passed of 147, typecheck exit 0. Optional refusal of one arm named twice declined: it prints two equal arms and no wrong number\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:92:- [x] T022 Cover the paired line of the text summary (`CTS` only). Lane S, after T021. This task adds one test case and changes no code: T021 prints a `paired` line in the text summary and no case reads it. Directly after the case `pairs two arms row by row`, add `it('prints the paired line in the text summary')`. Build the same eight log lines that case builds, write them to a log file in a temporary folder the way the helper `summarize` does, run `runScorer(['--summary', logPath, '--pair', 'pre,post'])` without `--json`, expect status 0 and expect its stdout to contain `paired pre to post: 4 rows, gained 1, lost 1, both followed 1, neither followed 1`. Remove the folder in a `finally`. The code already exists, so the first run passes. To show the case can fail, change the expected `gained 1` to `gained 2`, run it and see it fail, then restore `gained 1`. Verify: the deliberate run fails on the expected text, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 151 passed and 0 failed, and `G diff --quiet HEAD -- $S` is unchanged from before this task. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 151 passed as the code existed, the deliberate gained 2 run failed 1 of 151 on the expected text, restored 151 passed, no edit to the scorer. Shared-fixture extraction declined: two copies are not a pattern\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:40:This is **Phase 35** of the command surfacing build. It builds ranks 3 and 4 of research segment five. Ranks 1, 2 and 5 were declined until a full arm is designed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:106:- Turn duration, the OpenCode delivery receipt and a longer cap - declined until a full arm is designed\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:208:| REQ-012 | The B-5 trigger is evaluated from the printed counts and logged as fired, with B-5 handed to a new phase, or as declined with the counts. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:161:**Why.** D1 and D4 change what the scorer reads from a stored session, which the floors and eval never show. Phase 026's arm was stopped by the operator before scoring, so scoring it here would produce the verdict the operator declined.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:176:6. **The plugin timing test was fixed in T024.** The flake probe printed `18 passed, 2 failed of 20 runs, slowest process 820 ms` before, with the failure `expected bounded timeout, got 370ms`. T024's own run before its edit printed 16 passed and 4 failed. After the edit it printed `20 passed, 0 failed of 20 runs, slowest process 382 ms` (`scratch/repro-after.txt:170`). A bound on every scheduled delay was declined because a queue timer may run longer than 40 ms.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:177:7. **Smaller follow-ups declined on their task lines.** `stop here` plus a command reads as a refusal, accepted as rare (T005). A one-word path such as `/tmp` reads as a command with no colon, which no pattern can tell apart, and a file named like a command is too rare to earn a task (T026). A pin test on key order was declined because no reader emits both `command` and `cmd` (T028).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/goal.md:48:| D4 | A finding with no wrong output in a probe gets no code. The two skill label fallbacks and the plugin timing test are declined on their probe lines. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:62:- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `MENTION`, `OFFERS`, `CODEX $RL/runs-pre.jsonl`, `CODEX $RL/runs-post.jsonl`, `SHELL`, `node TSX $PL/probe-skill-label.mts` and `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20`, and write each command with its output into `repro-before.txt`. Verify: `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 40 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -e 'row 0: .* command=/(doctor:setup|create:changelog|speckit:resume) ' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 3, `rg -c -e '^shell events with no command text: (58|53)$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 2, `rg -c -F 'same head with and without the label: true' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '^termination grace test: 20 passed, 0 failed' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1. When the flake line reports a failed run, record the line in the parent goal log and plan no fix without a new task: the item was declined because it could not be shown. Evidence: scratch/repro-before.txt: SHIPPED 40 of 46 once, three row-0 command lines, both Codex lines 58 and 53, same head true. The flake line read 18 passed, 2 failed of 20 runs, recorded in the parent goal log.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:93:- [x] T024 [P] Check the scheduled termination delays instead of wall-clock time (`.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, test `termination grace stays inside the configured timeout budget`). Lane F, after T002, shares no file with another lane. This task edits that one test and nothing else, and it never edits the plugin itself. Under load the test failed 2 of 20 runs with `expected bounded timeout, got 370ms`, because timers fire late on a busy machine while the plugin still schedules its kill at the configured deadline. In the test, directly before `const output = await runPrompt(hooks);`, wrap `global.setTimeout` so each call pushes its delay argument onto a local array `delays` and then calls the original, and restore the original in a `finally` around `runPrompt`. After the call, add `assert.ok(delays.includes(40), ...)`, which states the plugin scheduled its kill at the configured 40 ms deadline, `assert.ok(!delays.includes(290), ...)`, which states the 250 ms grace was not added on top of it, and `assert.ok(delays.includes(0), ...)`, which states SIGTERM was scheduled at the deadline minus the grace, clamped at 0. Change `assert.ok(elapsedMs < 200, ...)` to `assert.ok(elapsedMs < 2000, ...)` with the same message, so the wall-clock check still catches the 2500 ms default. Add one comment saying the scheduled delays carry the budget check because timers fire late on a busy machine. Before the edit, run `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20` and record its counts (T002 saw 2 failed of 20). Verify: `node --test --test-name-pattern 'termination grace' .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`, `VP` reports `fail 0`, `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20` prints `20 passed, 0 failed` and `G diff --quiet BASE -- .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS: flake probe 16 passed 4 failed before, 20 passed 0 failed after. VP 45 of 45 fail 0. Plugin source unchanged against 60968af043. Follow-up every-delay bound declined: a queue timer may run longer than 40 ms\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:94:- [x] T025 Bind a later `run it` to the nearest command only (`CAT`, then `CA` function `commandOnlyMentioned`). Lane A, after T008. This task changes one expression in that function and nothing else in `CA`. The pronoun check T007 added reads the whole text after a command, so in `do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan, then run it for the auth module` the `it` meant for `/speckit:plan` makes `/speckit:complete` read as asked for. Test first: in `CAT`, add the row `['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan, then run it for the auth module', '/speckit:complete']` to the table of the case `still reads %s as a mention of %s`, run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see that row fail. Then in `commandOnlyMentioned`, test `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` against the part of the tail before the next slash command, `tail.split(/(?:^|[^a-z0-9_])\\/[a-z]/)[0]`, instead of the whole tail. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the two later-clause rows T007 added still pass, `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree` and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 1 failed (the new row), then 117 passed, the T007 rows pass, MENTION 46 of 46, typecheck exit 0. Gap: a path or URL before run it now hides the request, fixed by T026\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:97:- [x] T028 Read the `cmd` key of a Codex shell function call (`CTS`, then `S` constant `SHELL_COMMAND_KEYS`). Lane S, after T027. One constant and nothing else in `S`. A Codex `exec_command` function call carries its command under `cmd`, and `SHELL_COMMAND_KEYS` holds only `command`, so that step reaches the scorer with a null command and a read through it never counts as a load. Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('normalize')`, add `it('reads the cmd key of a Codex exec_command call')`, built with `normalize(oneTurn(toolCall('exec_command', { cmd: 'cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md' })), 'codex')`, expecting one event with `kind` `'shell'` and `command` `'cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md'`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the command read null. When `exec_command` does not map to the `shell` kind for codex, change nothing and mark the task `[B]` with the kind it maps to. Then change `SHELL_COMMAND_KEYS` to `Object.freeze(['command', 'cmd'])`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `maps the tool names $runtime registers` still passes and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 1 failed (command read null), then 165 passed, the six tool-name cases pass. Probe: command wins over cmd, other runtimes unchanged. A key-order pin test declined: no reader emits both keys\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:111:- [x] T023 [C] Write the results and close the phase (`$PH/implementation-summary.md`). Copy `$SP/implementation-summary.scaffold.md` to `$PH/implementation-summary.md` and fill it: `BASE` and `BASES`, the nine files, the six review prompts with their row 0 before and after, the Codex lines of `rescore-delta.txt`, every count that moved with its task, the items declined with the probe line behind each (the two skill label fallbacks and the relabel that waits on the operator), the plugin timing test fixed in T024 with the probe counts before and after and the limits the Codex numbers have (tuned rows, one run each, no brief delivered, a body with a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step). Mark each row of `acceptance-criteria.md` with the evidence observed, set the status in `spec.md` and the phase 24 row of `../spec.md` to `Complete`, then run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder $PH --apply`. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $PH --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`, `rg -c -e '^\\| codex ' $PH/implementation-summary.md` prints at least 1 and `rg -c \"\\| Unmet \\|\" $PH/acceptance-criteria.md` prints nothing. Evidence: Coordinator: implementation-summary.md written, AC 10 of 10 Met (Unmet search prints nothing), codex rows 7, spec Complete, parent row Complete, checklist P0 12 of 12 and P1 13 of 13 after the T009 first-run evidence and the neither-argument probe, strict RESULT: PASSED\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:200:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: finding 1 is `cross-consumer` (one producer, six readers), findings 4, 5 and the P022 reversal are `class-of-bug` in one reader of a prompt, finding 7 is `algorithmic`, finding 6 is `matrix/evidence`, finding 9 is declined and waits on the operator. Evidence: the finding table in `spec.md` and the parent goal log row that leaves finding 9 with the operator.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:212:| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The decline leads, the `not` word, the pronoun request and the sentence start |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:320:| Research | 10/20 | Every finding reproduced by a probe, three carry items declined on probe output |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md:101:- [x] T017 [P] Describe what the scorer prints (`S`). Replace the three header comment lines `// Reads a captured session through the shared session readers and reports what a`, ``// model did with the commands a turn offered it: the `COMMAND:` lines it printed,`` and `// the reads and writes in order, and whether a started loop ran its init first.` with `// Reads captured sessions through the shared session readers and prints counts`, `// and verdicts per runtime and arm: how often an offered command was started,` and `// seen or declined, which runs were unsafe and which started loops skipped their init.` Verify: `rg -c \"the reads and writes in order\" $S` prints nothing, `rg -c \"and verdicts per runtime and arm\" $S` prints 1 and `node --check $S` exits 0.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md:131:No task was marked `[B]`. Three follow-ups were declined, each on its task line: a rate-text assertion in T007, a refusal of one arm named twice in T018 and a shared-fixture extraction in T022.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:85:- [x] T007 [P] Print a range beside the followed rate and the load rate (`$CTS`, then `$S` functions `wilsonRange` and `tallyBlock`). Edit the functions in the order named, one at a time, and run the named test after each. Test first: add a `describe('wilsonRange')` block with the cases `wilsonRange(8, 16)` equals `{ low: 0.28, high: 0.72 }`, `wilsonRange(0, 16)` equals `{ low: 0, high: 0.19 }`, `wilsonRange(16, 16)` equals `{ low: 0.81, high: 1 }` and `wilsonRange(0, 0)` is `null`, and in `describe('run log summary')` add the case `prints a range beside each workflow rate`, which asserts the `workflow` block holds `followedRange` and `loadRange` equal to `wilsonRange` of each rate's two counts. They fail because `wilsonRange` is not exported. Then export `wilsonRange(successes, total)`, the Wilson score interval at 1.96 rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, and add the two fields to the `workflow` object in `tallyBlock`. `followedRate`, `loadRate` and `share` keep their text. Verify: `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports the new cases failed before the change and 0 failed after it. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run wilsonRange is not a function (5 failed), then 144 passed of 144. Typecheck exit 0. Optional rate-text assertion declined: the rate text and the range come from the same counts\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:88:- [x] T018 Refuse a pair the summary cannot use (`$CTS`, then `$S` function `selectMode`). After T009. This task changes the function `selectMode` and nothing else. Test first: add the case `refuses a pair without a summary or with one arm name`, which expects `runScorer(['--runtime', 'claude', '--locator', '{}', '--pair', 'pre,post'])` to exit with a status other than 0 and an error output that holds `--pair needs --summary`, and expects `runScorer(['--summary', 'missing-log.jsonl', '--pair', 'pre'])` to exit with a status other than 0 and an error output that holds `--pair needs two arm names`. It fails because neither message exists. Then in `selectMode`, inside the `if (options.summaryLogs !== null)` block before `return 'summary';`, throw `new UsageError('--pair needs two arm names, as <from>,<to>')` when `options.pair` is a string that does not split on `,` into exactly two non-empty names. After that block, before the `--runtime` check, throw `new UsageError('--pair needs --summary')` when `options.pair` is not `null`. Verify: the file reports the new case failed before the change and 0 failed after it. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run missing --pair needs --summary (1 failed), then 147 passed of 147, typecheck exit 0. Optional refusal of one arm named twice declined: it prints two equal arms and no wrong number\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:92:- [x] T022 Cover the paired line of the text summary (`CTS` only). Lane S, after T021. This task adds one test case and changes no code: T021 prints a `paired` line in the text summary and no case reads it. Directly after the case `pairs two arms row by row`, add `it('prints the paired line in the text summary')`. Build the same eight log lines that case builds, write them to a log file in a temporary folder the way the helper `summarize` does, run `runScorer(['--summary', logPath, '--pair', 'pre,post'])` without `--json`, expect status 0 and expect its stdout to contain `paired pre to post: 4 rows, gained 1, lost 1, both followed 1, neither followed 1`. Remove the folder in a `finally`. The code already exists, so the first run passes. To show the case can fail, change the expected `gained 1` to `gained 2`, run it and see it fail, then restore `gained 1`. Verify: the deliberate run fails on the expected text, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 151 passed and 0 failed, and `G diff --quiet HEAD -- $S` is unchanged from before this task. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 151 passed as the code existed, the deliberate gained 2 run failed 1 of 151 on the expected text, restored 151 passed, no edit to the scorer. Shared-fixture extraction declined: two copies are not a pattern\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:40:This is **Phase 35** of the command surfacing build. It builds ranks 3 and 4 of research segment five. Ranks 1, 2 and 5 were declined until a full arm is designed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:106:- Turn duration, the OpenCode delivery receipt and a longer cap - declined until a full arm is designed\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:208:| REQ-012 | The B-5 trigger is evaluated from the printed counts and logged as fired, with B-5 handed to a new phase, or as declined with the counts. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:161:**Why.** D1 and D4 change what the scorer reads from a stored session, which the floors and eval never show. Phase 026's arm was stopped by the operator before scoring, so scoring it here would produce the verdict the operator declined.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:176:6. **The plugin timing test was fixed in T024.** The flake probe printed `18 passed, 2 failed of 20 runs, slowest process 820 ms` before, with the failure `expected bounded timeout, got 370ms`. T024's own run before its edit printed 16 passed and 4 failed. After the edit it printed `20 passed, 0 failed of 20 runs, slowest process 382 ms` (`scratch/repro-after.txt:170`). A bound on every scheduled delay was declined because a queue timer may run longer than 40 ms.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:177:7. **Smaller follow-ups declined on their task lines.** `stop here` plus a command reads as a refusal, accepted as rare (T005). A one-word path such as `/tmp` reads as a command with no colon, which no pattern can tell apart, and a file named like a command is too rare to earn a task (T026). A pin test on key order was declined because no reader emits both `command` and `cmd` (T028).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/goal.md:48:| D4 | A finding with no wrong output in a probe gets no code. The two skill label fallbacks and the plugin timing test are declined on their probe lines. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:62:- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `MENTION`, `OFFERS`, `CODEX $RL/runs-pre.jsonl`, `CODEX $RL/runs-post.jsonl`, `SHELL`, `node TSX $PL/probe-skill-label.mts` and `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20`, and write each command with its output into `repro-before.txt`. Verify: `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 40 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -e 'row 0: .* command=/(doctor:setup|create:changelog|speckit:resume) ' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 3, `rg -c -e '^shell events with no command text: (58|53)$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 2, `rg -c -F 'same head with and without the label: true' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '^termination grace test: 20 passed, 0 failed' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1. When the flake line reports a failed run, record the line in the parent goal log and plan no fix without a new task: the item was declined because it could not be shown. Evidence: scratch/repro-before.txt: SHIPPED 40 of 46 once, three row-0 command lines, both Codex lines 58 and 53, same head true. The flake line read 18 passed, 2 failed of 20 runs, recorded in the parent goal log.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:93:- [x] T024 [P] Check the scheduled termination delays instead of wall-clock time (`.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, test `termination grace stays inside the configured timeout budget`). Lane F, after T002, shares no file with another lane. This task edits that one test and nothing else, and it never edits the plugin itself. Under load the test failed 2 of 20 runs with `expected bounded timeout, got 370ms`, because timers fire late on a busy machine while the plugin still schedules its kill at the configured deadline. In the test, directly before `const output = await runPrompt(hooks);`, wrap `global.setTimeout` so each call pushes its delay argument onto a local array `delays` and then calls the original, and restore the original in a `finally` around `runPrompt`. After the call, add `assert.ok(delays.includes(40), ...)`, which states the plugin scheduled its kill at the configured 40 ms deadline, `assert.ok(!delays.includes(290), ...)`, which states the 250 ms grace was not added on top of it, and `assert.ok(delays.includes(0), ...)`, which states SIGTERM was scheduled at the deadline minus the grace, clamped at 0. Change `assert.ok(elapsedMs < 200, ...)` to `assert.ok(elapsedMs < 2000, ...)` with the same message, so the wall-clock check still catches the 2500 ms default. Add one comment saying the scheduled delays carry the budget check because timers fire late on a busy machine. Before the edit, run `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20` and record its counts (T002 saw 2 failed of 20). Verify: `node --test --test-name-pattern 'termination grace' .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`, `VP` reports `fail 0`, `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20` prints `20 passed, 0 failed` and `G diff --quiet BASE -- .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS: flake probe 16 passed 4 failed before, 20 passed 0 failed after. VP 45 of 45 fail 0. Plugin source unchanged against 60968af043. Follow-up every-delay bound declined: a queue timer may run longer than 40 ms\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:94:- [x] T025 Bind a later `run it` to the nearest command only (`CAT`, then `CA` function `commandOnlyMentioned`). Lane A, after T008. This task changes one expression in that function and nothing else in `CA`. The pronoun check T007 added reads the whole text after a command, so in `do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan, then run it for the auth module` the `it` meant for `/speckit:plan` makes `/speckit:complete` read as asked for. Test first: in `CAT`, add the row `['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan, then run it for the auth module', '/speckit:complete']` to the table of the case `still reads %s as a mention of %s`, run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see that row fail. Then in `commandOnlyMentioned`, test `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` against the part of the tail before the next slash command, `tail.split(/(?:^|[^a-z0-9_])\\/[a-z]/)[0]`, instead of the whole tail. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the two later-clause rows T007 added still pass, `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree` and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 1 failed (the new row), then 117 passed, the T007 rows pass, MENTION 46 of 46, typecheck exit 0. Gap: a path or URL before run it now hides the request, fixed by T026\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:97:- [x] T028 Read the `cmd` key of a Codex shell function call (`CTS`, then `S` constant `SHELL_COMMAND_KEYS`). Lane S, after T027. One constant and nothing else in `S`. A Codex `exec_command` function call carries its command under `cmd`, and `SHELL_COMMAND_KEYS` holds only `command`, so that step reaches the scorer with a null command and a read through it never counts as a load. Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('normalize')`, add `it('reads the cmd key of a Codex exec_command call')`, built with `normalize(oneTurn(toolCall('exec_command', { cmd: 'cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md' })), 'codex')`, expecting one event with `kind` `'shell'` and `command` `'cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md'`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the command read null. When `exec_command` does not map to the `shell` kind for codex, change nothing and mark the task `[B]` with the kind it maps to. Then change `SHELL_COMMAND_KEYS` to `Object.freeze(['command', 'cmd'])`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `maps the tool names $runtime registers` still passes and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 1 failed (command read null), then 165 passed, the six tool-name cases pass. Probe: command wins over cmd, other runtimes unchanged. A key-order pin test declined: no reader emits both keys\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:111:- [x] T023 [C] Write the results and close the phase (`$PH/implementation-summary.md`). Copy `$SP/implementation-summary.scaffold.md` to `$PH/implementation-summary.md` and fill it: `BASE` and `BASES`, the nine files, the six review prompts with their row 0 before and after, the Codex lines of `rescore-delta.txt`, every count that moved with its task, the items declined with the probe line behind each (the two skill label fallbacks and the relabel that waits on the operator), the plugin timing test fixed in T024 with the probe counts before and after and the limits the Codex numbers have (tuned rows, one run each, no brief delivered, a body with a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step). Mark each row of `acceptance-criteria.md` with the evidence observed, set the status in `spec.md` and the phase 24 row of `../spec.md` to `Complete`, then run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder $PH --apply`. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $PH --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`, `rg -c -e '^\\| codex ' $PH/implementation-summary.md` prints at least 1 and `rg -c \"\\| Unmet \\|\" $PH/acceptance-criteria.md` prints nothing. Evidence: Coordinator: implementation-summary.md written, AC 10 of 10 Met (Unmet search prints nothing), codex rows 7, spec Complete, parent row Complete, checklist P0 12 of 12 and P1 13 of 13 after the T009 first-run evidence and the neither-argument probe, strict RESULT: PASSED\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:200:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: finding 1 is `cross-consumer` (one producer, six readers), findings 4, 5 and the P022 reversal are `class-of-bug` in one reader of a prompt, finding 7 is `algorithmic`, finding 6 is `matrix/evidence`, finding 9 is declined and waits on the operator. Evidence: the finding table in `spec.md` and the parent goal log row that leaves finding 9 with the operator.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:212:| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The decline leads, the `not` word, the pronoun request and the sentence start |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:320:| Research | 10/20 | Every finding reproduced by a probe, three carry items declined on probe output |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md:101:- [x] T017 [P] Describe what the scorer prints (`S`). Replace the three header comment lines `// Reads a captured session through the shared session readers and reports what a`, ``// model did with the commands a turn offered it: the `COMMAND:` lines it printed,`` and `// the reads and writes in order, and whether a started loop ran its init first.` with `// Reads captured sessions through the shared session readers and prints counts`, `// and verdicts per runtime and arm: how often an offered command was started,` and `// seen or declined, which runs were unsafe and which started loops skipped their init.` Verify: `rg -c \"the reads and writes in order\" $S` prints nothing, `rg -c \"and verdicts per runtime and arm\" $S` prints 1 and `node --check $S` exits 0.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"do not run it\\\\|declined\\\\|pronoun\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --include=\\\"*.md\\\" | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794868738141,"end":1794868738931}}}}
