{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794868776230,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e683c319001bDh1VN1HvHxcJB","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e683b28a001z3SAYOyOXOG73f","type":"tool","id":"call_154b805314404685965ea7f2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"run it twice\\|command file, then run it\\|never run it without\" specs --include=\"*.md\" | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md:17:| mention-13 F002 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | \"don't run it twice\" and \"never run it without a budget\" read as refusals | Fixed: the refusal has to end its clause; two cases fail on the old code |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:20:1. A command named as a document now reads as a mention even when the same prompt then asks to run it, so `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` loses the command the reader typed (F001).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:21:2. A limiting negation after the name now reads as a refusal, so `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` loses the command too (F002).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:79:    \"Record that a later request clause outranks a document naming, and that a qualified negation (`don't run it twice`) is a limit rather than a refusal.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:82:    \"Add a failing-first test for `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` and for `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff`.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:83:    \"Add a failing-first test for `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget`.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:109:- Impact: `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` yields `typedCommandForTop(...) === undefined`; `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff` yields `attachCommand(...) === undefined` even though `thorough` matches `DEPTH_REQUEST`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:111:- Scope proof: exported guards and consumer run on both prompts; both classify as mentions, and the unchanged pronoun regex matches the tail `command file, then run it`, so the earlier read was a request.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/review-report.md:118:- Impact: `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget` lose the typed command.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-001.md:34:1. **A document naming returns a mention before a later request clause is read** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:458` -- `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` returns `true` from `commandOnlyMentioned` on the document noun alone, so the `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` check at line 460 never runs for that occurrence. `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` reads as a mention, and `typedCommandForTop('system-deep-loop', ...)` returns `undefined` for a prompt that literally asks to run the command. The same shadowing withholds a hub command the reader asked for: `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE('review'), 'read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff')` returns `undefined` although `DEPTH_REQUEST` matches `thorough` at line 323. The function's own contract at lines 403-407 says a clause that opens with a use verb and `it` turns an earlier naming into a request, and the diff placed the new early return ahead of it.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-001.md:36:   Scope proof: Ran the exported `commandOnlyMentioned` and `typedCommandForTop` on the two prompts above; both classify as mentions. The old tree had no `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT` return, and the unchanged pronoun regex matches the tail `command file, then run it`, so the earlier read was a request. `REQUEST6`/`CONTROL5` do not carry a document naming, which is why the suite stays green.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-001.md:38:   Case: `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` typed by a reader who wants the review run, and `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff` on a hub route to the review mode.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-001.md:59:2. **A limiting negation after the name reads as a refusal** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:413` -- `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` ends at `it\\b`, so any qualifier after `it` still satisfies the refusal: `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` reads as a mention, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', ...)` returns `undefined`, and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget` does the same on the hub path. The comment at lines 409-412 claims the rule keeps a request a request, and the packet records this exact risk as High at `spec.md:150` with `REQUEST6`, `CONTROL5` and the wrapper matrix as the mitigation; none of those rows carries a limiting clause after `it`, so the mitigation does not cover the shape it names.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-001.md:63:   Case: `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice`, and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget`, both typed requests with a limit rather than a refusal.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-001.md:77:  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"`don't run it twice` could be read as refusing the second run, which is still a refusal of a run. Rejected as the intended reading here: the clause limits a run the reader already asked for, and the function's stated job is to keep a request a request.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-001.md:117:- Ambiguity: `don't run it twice` (F002) is the one place where a reader could argue the negation is a refusal. It is recorded at P1 with a downgrade trigger rather than assumed; the mirror prompt `don't skip it`, which the packet pins at `spec.md:178`, still reads as a request.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-005.md:53:- F001 reproduces: `open the /deep:review command file, then run it` and `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff` both read as mentions.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-13/iterations/iteration-005.md:54:- F002 reproduces: `run /speckit:save and don't run it twice` and `run /deep:review but never run it without a budget` both read as mentions.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/implementation-summary.md:83:| A refusa