{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794868986134,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e6873c58001TQcLcptKLUWhPy","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e6871ff7001hTBjwBJHa21VAj","type":"tool","id":"call_91c7b1319c2f4fa0ba53741f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '50,62p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md; echo \"--- summary 78-90\"; sed -n '78,90p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/implementation-summary.md; echo \"--- tasks 40-50\"; sed -n '40,50p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md"},"output":"\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nA reader who refuses or questions a command still gets it offered in four shapes: a refusal after the name (\"/create:readme is not what I want, do not run it\"), the command named as a document (\"read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does\"), a wrapper the fold keeps such as `[/create:readme]`, and a doc path such as `/create:readme.md` beside a led refusal. One playbook scenario pins a prompt that no longer tops `/doctor:update`. Four advisor tasks, a stale skill graph rebuild, the Vibe prompt hook setup and the behaviour arena, rank another skill or none first.\n\n### Purpose\nA refused or questioned command is never offered in those shapes, a request still is, the playbook passes as written, and the four advisor tasks rank the advisor first without moving the floors.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n--- summary 78-90\n\n| Decision | Why |\n|----------|-----|\n| A document naming needs a determiner | A typed request puts its argument after the name, as in `/create:diff file a.md b.md`, while \"read the /create:readme document\" names it |\n| Decline probes P05, P08 and P09 (ADR-001) | `/doctor:helper` ranks `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first for P05. P08 and P09 needed common words that pulled ordinary prompts to the advisor |\n| A refusal of \"it\" must end its clause, and a later request clause is read first | \"don't run it twice\" limits a run and \"read the docs, then run it\" asks for one, review pass thirteen |\n| Drop the wrapper marks everywhere, not only next to a name | They carry no lead word, so dropping them changes no lead reading, and the invariance matrix checks every fixture |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:verification -->\n## Verification\n--- tasks 40-50\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [x] T002 Add the failing cases first (`$ADV/GUARDS`). Verify: they fail on `b8ebee37d75`. Evidence: 16 new cases fail on b8ebee37d75: six wrapper pairs in the matrix, three later refusals, two document namings, the doc path and four typed wrappers\n- [x] T003 Read a refusal after the name and a command named as a document (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`). After T002. Verify: the E-1 and D1 cases pass and REQUEST6 and CONTROL5 stay requests. Evidence: a refusal of it after the name and a command named as a document after the, this or that read as mentions; the first document rule also caught three typed rows whose argument follows the name, so it now needs a determiner; rule-diag.mjs read those rows by id; the argument guard passes\n- [x] T004 Drop the wider wrapper set, skip a doc-path occurrence and widen the typed start boundary (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`). After T002. Verify: the wrapper matrix and the path case pass. Evidence: the fold drops brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes; the occurrence scan skips a doc path; the typed start boundary takes the same marks; the wrapper matrix and the typed cases pass\n- [x] T005 Change the playbook's third prompt (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md`). Verify: the Claude hook names `/doctor:update` for it. Evidence: the third prompt is now check for skilled updates; the Claude hook prints /doctor:update (ask) in a parent session and (parent-named only) in a child\n- [x] T006 Add advisor intent phrases for the four probe tasks and recompile the graph (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `$ADV/scripts/skill-graph.json`). Verify: `run-probes.cjs` tops system-skill-advisor for the four, `FLOOR` and `EVAL` unchanged. Evidence: seven phrases appended to the advisor intent_signals, graph recompiled and rescanned; P07, P08 and P09 top system-skill-advisor; P05 is declined: /doctor:helper ranks /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild first for it, the right repair; FLOOR and EVAL unchanged\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nA reader who refuses or questions a command still gets it offered in four shapes: a refusal after the name (\"/create:readme is not what I want, do not run it\"), the command named as a document (\"read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does\"), a wrapper the fold keeps such as `[/create:readme]`, and a doc path such as `/create:readme.md` beside a led refusal. One playbook scenario pins a prompt that no longer tops `/doctor:update`. Four advisor tasks, a stale skill graph rebuild, the Vibe prompt hook setup and the behaviour arena, rank another skill or none first.\n\n### Purpose\nA refused or questioned command is never offered in those shapes, a request still is, the playbook passes as written, and the four advisor tasks rank the advisor first without moving the floors.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n--- summary 78-90\n\n| Decision | Why |\n|----------|-----|\n| A document naming needs a determiner | A typed request puts its argument after the name, as in `/create:diff file a.md b.md`, while \"read the /create:readme document\" names it |\n| Decline probes P05, P08 and P09 (ADR-001) | `/doctor:helper` ranks `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first for P05. P08 and P09 needed common words that pulled ordinary prompts to the advisor |\n| A refusal of \"it\" must end its clause, and a later request clause is read first | \"don't run it twice\" limits a run and \"read the docs, then run it\" asks for one, review pass thirteen |\n| Drop the wrapper marks everywhere, not only next to a name | They carry no lead word, so dropping them changes no lead reading, and the invariance matrix checks every fixture |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:verification -->\n## Verification\n--- tasks 40-50\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [x] T002 Add the failing cases first (`$ADV/GUARDS`). Verify: they fail on `b8ebee37d75`. Evidence: 16 new cases fail on b8ebee37d75: six wrapper pairs in the matrix, three later refusals, two document namings, the doc path and four typed wrappers\n- [x] T003 Read a refusal after the name and a command named as a document (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`). After T002. Verify: the E-1 and D1 cases pass and REQUEST6 and CONTROL5 stay requests. Evidence: a refusal of it after the name and a command named as a document after the, this or that read as mentions; the first document rule also caught three typed rows whose argument follows the name, so it now needs a determiner; rule-diag.mjs read those rows by id; the argument guard passes\n- [x] T004 Drop the wider wrapper set, skip a doc-path occurrence and widen the typed start boundary (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`). After T002. Verify: the wrapper matrix and the path case pass. Evidence: the fold drops brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes; the occurrence scan skips a doc path; the typed start boundary takes the same marks; the wrapper matrix and the typed cases pass\n- [x] T005 Change the playbook's third prompt (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md`). Verify: the Claude hook names `/doctor:update` for it. Evidence: the third prompt is now check for skilled updates; the Claude hook prints /doctor:update (ask) in a parent session and (parent-named only) in a child\n- [x] T006 Add advisor intent phrases for the four probe tasks and recompile the graph (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `$ADV/scripts/skill-graph.json`). Verify: `run-probes.cjs` tops system-skill-advisor for the four, `FLOOR` and `EVAL` unchanged. Evidence: seven phrases appended to the advisor intent_signals, graph recompiled and rescanned; P07, P08 and P09 top system-skill-advisor; P05 is declined: /doctor:helper ranks /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild first for it, the right repair; FLOOR and EVAL unchanged\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '50,62p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md; echo \\\"--- summary 78-90\\\"; sed -n '78,90p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/implementation-summary.md; echo \\\"--- tasks 40-50\\\"; sed -n '40,50p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794868984920,"end":1794868986134}}}}
