time/lib/command-attach.ts:415\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"correctness-regression\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"Ran the exported guard and consumer on five prompts; all return the request reading. The removed pattern ended at it\\\\b, so the same inputs read as mentions before this branch.\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"commandOnlyMentioned:463\", \"typedCommandForTop:259\", \"attachCommand:533\"],\n      \"type\": \"behavioral\",\n      \"claim\": \"A refusal after the name whose object is followed by a reason or a repeat adverb is read as a request, so a mutating command is offered against the refusal.\",\n      \"evidenceRefs\": [\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:415\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:463\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:533\"\n      ],\n      \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Checked the leading decline leads for a refusal before the name; the refusal here is after it. Checked the ask-by-pronoun and document rules; neither matches. The new fixtures carry no trailing reason.\",\n      \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The author may read any qualifier after it as a limit, as with don't run it twice. Rejected for again and because: the clause refuses the run and the prompt has no request.\",\n      \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.94,\n      \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade if a corpus shows a prompt of this shape whose author meant to run the command.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-P1-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"A document naming followed by any then clause is read as a request\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"rule-precedence\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"Ran the guard and consumer on four prompts; the document naming returns a mention without then and a request with it. The pronoun rule already carries '... then run it', so the guard only adds read-only follow-ups.\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"attachCommand:533\", \"attachCommand:549-552\", \"COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT:423\"],\n      \"type\": \"behavioral\",\n      \"claim\": \"A prompt that names a command as a document and then asks a read-only or unrelated follow-up is read as a request for the command.\",\n      \"evidenceRefs\": [\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:423\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:549\"\n      ],\n      \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Checked whether the pronoun rule needs the then guard: it already matches ', then run it'. Checked the determiner and occurrence boundaries; both pass for 'the /deep:review command file'.\",\n      \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The guard may intend any then clause to mark work. Rejected because then tell me and then run the test suite ask for something other than the named command.\",\n      \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.93,\n      \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade if the accepted reading is that any then clause in a prompt naming the command is a request for it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-P2-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The new fixtures pin neither boundary the two rules changed\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:210\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"test-coverage-gap\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"Read both fixture tables at 202-218 and 221-229; the only then row asserts a request and the only post-name refusals end at it.\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"tests:210-218\", \"REFUSE8:42-51\", \"document table:221-226\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"traceabilityChecks\": { \"results\": [] },\n  \"newFindingsRatio\": 1.0,\n  \"noveltyJustification\": \"All three findings are new to this lineage: two P1s on the two changed rules and one P2 on the fixtures. No refinement rows.\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-mention-14-1794868189353-tsxtos\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T22:44:50Z\",\n  \"durationMs\": 470000,\n  \"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"reviewDepthApplicability\": {\n    \"scopeClass\": \"standard\",\n    \"enforcement\": \"strict\",\n    \"reason\": \"Two runtime files govern whether a mutating command is offered; not a trivial target and not a whole-skill audit.\",\n    \"evidenceRefs\": [\n      \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:442\",\n      \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:138\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"targetSelection\": {\n    \"selectedTargets\": [\n      \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\",\n      \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"selectionReason\": \"Both are the pass-fourteen scope files for the mention area; the guard and its fixtures are the whole produced surface of the two changed rules.\",\n    \"discoveryMethods\": [\"direct_read\", \"exact_search\", \"negative_test_inspection\"],\n    \"omittedHighRiskTargets\": [],\n    \"graphStatus\": \"available\",\n    \"semanticSearchStatus\": \"unavailable\",\n    \"evidenceRefs\": [\n      \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-14.txt:2-3\",\n      \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:442\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"searchCoverage\": {\n    \"requiredBugClasses\": [\"rule_precedence\", \"clause_boundary\", \"test_boundary_pinning\", \"ty