{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869390041,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e68d329e0020FPY5pNGU74qOy","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e68d268b001LHu8ZAAzH6rW7t","type":"tool","id":"call_cdef9e89c2514c8e895640c9","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 002 - security\n\n## Dimension\n\nSecurity: the guard sits on the boundary between untrusted prompt text and a recommendation that can carry a mutating command. This pass asks whether prompt text can steer the guard through pattern construction, backtracking, or markup folding.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n```text\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\nBINDING: mode=review\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n```\n\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\n\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The security pass stayed on the two `mention` scope files and honored the holdout rule: no corpus or holdout file was opened, no forbidden diff was run, and no session text was read.\n\nSources: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-572`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1-621`, `review-brief-14.txt:1-10`, `review-scope-14.txt:1-5`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-572`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1-621`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-14.txt:1-10`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-14.txt:1-5`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\nNot run in this iteration; the traceability pass is iteration 3.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `commandOnlyMentioned` is exported and reached from two consumers in the same file: `typedCommandForTop` (`command-attach.ts:259`) and `attachCommand` (`command-attach.ts:533`). Both feed a command whose `policy` can be `start` or `ask`, so a wrong mention reading changes what the reader is offered.\n- `typedCommandIn` (`command-attach.ts:221-245`) is the only other prompt-text matcher on this path; it does not build a pattern from prompt text at all.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The fold at `command-attach.ts:443-451` removes brackets, parentheses, quotes, guillemets, primes and code tags before the rules run. That is deliberate: a refusal wrapped in any of them still reads as a refusal (verified on four wrapped prompts). It cannot be used to hide a refusal, because removing the wrapper exposes the lead rather than the reverse.\n- The occurrence regex is rebuilt per call, but only from static vocabulary plus `escapePhrase`d command names; the prompt contributes no pattern text.\n- A 400,025-character prompt with a trailing refusal completed in 11 ms; 400,016 characters of `and ` repetitions, 200,000 slashes, and 200,000 dots each completed in 6 ms or less. No nested-quantifier blowup was found on the looked-for classes.\n- Trust boundary: `commandOnlyMentioned` takes the raw prompt, so every value the prompt can send is in reach (`review-core.md` reach calibration). The only effect is the boolean reading; no code execution, file access, or network use exists on this path.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Every `new RegExp` site (`command-attach.ts:323, 327, 407, 415, 456, 466, 468, 470, 473, 480`) builds from static text, or from `escapePhrase`d command spellings, or from the shared `COMMAND_OR_LIST` vocabulary. No prompt substring is interpolated unescaped.\n- The two changed patterns (`415`, `465`) are static regexes with only optional groups; no unbounded repetition over prompt-derived alternatives.\n- `COMMAND_OR_LIST` is a fixed pattern built from `[a-z]` classes, and the lead lists are constants.\n- The suite's wrapper matrix (`tests:175-189`) already asserts that every fixture reads the same wrapped as plain, which is the security-relevant invariance for the fold.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Regex injection through a command name: `escapePhrase` (`command-attach.ts:316-318`) escapes every metacharacter; both the occurrence regex and the determiner regex use the result.\n- Backtracking denial of service on long or repetitive prompts: measured at 11 ms for 400k characters on the worst tried shape; the alternations are literal and bounded.\n- Markup folding used to turn a refusal into a request: the fold strips the wrapper, and a wrapped refusal still returns a mention (`(do not run /create:readme)`, `[do not run /create:readme]`, `**never use /create:readme**`, `` `what does /create:readme do?` ``).\n- Consent bypass in the fold: the guard's output only withholds or allows the offer; the refusal misreads are carried as correctness at `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002`, and no separate security defect was found.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: the pass-thirteen decision record and the phase-040 problem statement against the two changed rules; record `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence`.\n- Reason: correctness found two behavior gaps; the traceability pass must say whether the recorded claims are consistent with what was implemented.\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no exhausted approaches.\n- Required evidence: `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md` problem statement, `implementation-summary.md` decision row, and the task evidence line for the two fixes.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo finding in this dimension; the two P1s from iteration 1 remain active but are not security defects.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 002 - security\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nSecurity: the guard sits on the boundary between untrusted prompt text and a recommendation that can carry a mutating command. This pass asks whether prompt text can steer the guard through pattern construction, backtracking, or markup folding.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n```text\\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\\nBINDING: mode=review\\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\n```\\n\\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\\n\\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The security pass stayed on the two `mention` scope files and honored the holdout rule: no corpus or holdout file was opened, no forbidden diff was run, and no session text was read.\\n\\nSources: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-572`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1-621`, `review-brief-14.txt:1-10`, `review-scope-14.txt:1-5`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-572`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1-621`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-14.txt:1-10`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-14.txt:1-5`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\nNot run in this iteration; the traceability pass is iteration 3.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `commandOnlyMentioned` is exported and reached from two consumers in the same file: `typedCommandForTop` (`command-attach.ts:259`) and `attachCommand` (`command-attach.ts:533`). Both feed a command whose `policy` can be `start` or `ask`, so a wrong mention reading changes what the reader is offered.\\n- `typedCommandIn` (`command-attach.ts:221-245`) is the only other prompt-text matcher on this path; it does not build a pattern from prompt text at all.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The fold at `command-attach.ts:443-451` removes brackets, parentheses, quotes, guillemets, primes and code tags before the rules run. That is deliberate: a refusal wrapped in any of them still reads as a refusal (verified on four wrapped prompts). It cannot be used to hide a refusal, because removing the wrapper exposes the lead rather than the reverse.\\n- The occurrence regex is rebuilt per call, but only from static vocabulary plus `escapePhrase`d command names; the prompt contributes no pattern text.\\n- A 400,025-character prompt with a trailing refusal completed in 11 ms; 400,016 characters of `and ` repetitions, 200,000 slashes, and 200,000 dots each completed in 6 ms or less. No nested-quantifier blowup was found on the looked-for classes.\\n- Trust boundary: `commandOnlyMentioned` takes the raw prompt, so every value the prompt can send is in reach (`review-core.md` reach calibration). The only effect is the boolean reading; no code execution, file access, or network use exists on this path.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Every `new RegExp` site (`command-attach.ts:323, 327, 407, 415, 456, 466, 468, 470, 473, 480`) builds from static text, or from `escapePhrase`d command spellings, or from the shared `COMMAND_OR_LIST` vocabulary. No prompt substring is interpolated unescaped.\\n- The two changed patterns (`415`, `465`) are static regexes with only optional groups; no unbounded repetition over prompt-derived alternatives.\\n- `COMMAND_OR_LIST` is a fixed pattern built from `[a-z]` classes, and the lead lists are constants.\\n- The suite's wrapper matrix (`tests:175-189`) already asserts that every fixture reads the same wrapped as plain, which is the security-relevant invariance for the fold.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Regex injection through a command name: `escapePhrase` (`command-attach.ts:316-318`) escapes every metacharacter; both the occurrence regex and the determiner regex use the result.\\n- Backtracking denial of service on long or repetitive prompts: measured at 11 ms for 400k characters on the worst tried shape; the alternations are literal and bounded.\\n- Markup folding used to turn a refusal into a request: the fold strips the wrapper, and a wrapped refusal still returns a mention (`(do not run /create:readme)`, `[do not run /create:readme]`, `**never use /create:readme**`, `` `what does /create:readme do?` ``).\\n- Consent bypass in the fold: the guard's output only withholds or allows the offer; the refusal misreads are carried as correctness at `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002`, and no separate security defect was found.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: the pass-thirteen decision record and the phase-040 problem statement against the two changed rules; record `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence`.\\n- Reason: correctness found two behavior gaps; the traceability pass must say whether the recorded claims are consistent with what was implemented.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no exhausted approaches.\\n- Required evidence: `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md` problem statement, `implementation-summary.md` decision row, and the task evidence line for the two fixes.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo finding in this dimension; the two P1s from iteration 1 remain active but are not security defects.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869375646,"end":1794869390041}}}}
