{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869768916,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e692ff900020hSTYEg8GRhve6","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e692dd27001lg1iWsvApB1x9C","type":"tool","id":"call_cd93ba71a8ba49c5b3784b6d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 005 - correctness replay\n\n## Dimension\n\nCorrectness, replay: re-run both P1 reproductions line by line and sweep the two boundaries, so each active finding stays grounded in observed behavior rather than stale prose. Recovery granularity: line level.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n```text\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\nBINDING: mode=review\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n```\n\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\n\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The replay stayed inside the two scope files and honored the holdout rule.\n\nRecovery note: the iteration-4 stop decision was again `STUCK_RECOVERY` (stuckCount 3). This replay follows the recovery strategy's protocol replay step and keeps the P1s active.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:403-482`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:200-218`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-14.txt:1-10`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002` remain active and reproduce.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. `R1-P2-001` remains active.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\nNot re-run; iteration 3's `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence` results stand.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `R1-P1-001` replay: `commandOnlyMentioned('/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again', '/create:readme')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)` returns `/create:readme`. Same for `anymore`, `because it is broken`, `until it is fixed`, `today`, `ever again`.\n- `R1-P1-002` replay: `commandOnlyMentioned('read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does', '/deep:review')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE('review'), prompt)` returns `/deep:review`. Same for `then summarize it`, `then check the changelog`, `then run the test suite`.\n- Boundary sweep of the allowed trailing words: `yet`, `now`, `for now`, `at all`, `please` all keep the mention reading, which matches the change's stated allowlist. `twice` reads as a request, which is the intended pass-thirteen trade-off.\n- Boundary sweep of `then`: only `then do a thorough review of this diff` and `then run it` are genuine requests; every other probed `then` clause is read as a request although it asks for something else.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `do not run it today` reads as a request. That is a time limit rather than a refusal, so it is consistent with the change's limit/refusal distinction; it is not counted as part of `R1-P1-001`.\n- `do not run it twice` reads as a request, the intended behavior. It stays out of the finding.\n- A refusal ending in `ever again` fails for the same anchor reason as `again`; folded into `R1-P1-001`, not raised separately.\n- A `then` clause that names the command again (`then run it`) is a request through the pronoun rule as well as the `then` guard; the guard is not what decides it.\n- No prompt was found in these two rules where a request reads as a mention beyond the intended limits, so the opposite direction stays clean.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The five-word allowlist behaves exactly as written: all five keep a mention.\n- The two P1 prompts still return the wrong reading on the current tree (working tree matches `e626653ce79`), so neither finding is stale.\n- The consumer still offers the command for each failing prompt, so both findings have a reachable effect.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Downgrading `R1-P1-001` because `again` can imply a previous run: the probe uses `keeps failing` and `is broken`, where the clause refuses a further run and the prompt contains no request.\n- Downgrading `R1-P1-002` because `then` often introduces work: five of six probed `then` clauses ask for a read or a different task, so the word alone is not a request marker.\n- A new finding for `today`: it is a limit, not a refusal, and the change's own comment names limits as requests.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness (consumer cross-reference)\n- Focus area: `typedCommandForTop`, `attachCommand` and `routeNeedsMode`, plus the generated `MODE_COMMANDS`/`COMMAND_ROWS`/`TRACKED_COMMANDS` consistency for the two commands in the probes.\n- Reason: the replay confirmed the guard; the next pass asks whether a consumer could still deliver the wrong command through a different path or a table mismatch.\n- Rotation status: four dimensions covered; consumer cross-reference next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the traceability gate stays closed; expect another recovery or continue decision, not STOP.\n- Required evidence: consumer return values for a mention and a request prompt, and own-key/table agreement for `/deep:review` and `/create:readme`.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo new finding; both P1s and the P2 remain active and reproduce.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 005 - correctness replay\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nCorrectness, replay: re-run both P1 reproductions line by line and sweep the two boundaries, so each active finding stays grounded in observed behavior rather than stale prose. Recovery granularity: line level.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n```text\\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\\nBINDING: mode=review\\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\n```\\n\\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\\n\\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The replay stayed inside the two scope files and honored the holdout rule.\\n\\nRecovery note: the iteration-4 stop decision was again `STUCK_RECOVERY` (stuckCount 3). This replay follows the recovery strategy's protocol replay step and keeps the P1s active.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:403-482`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:200-218`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-14.txt:1-10`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002` remain active and reproduce.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. `R1-P2-001` remains active.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\nNot re-run; iteration 3's `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence` results stand.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `R1-P1-001` replay: `commandOnlyMentioned('/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again', '/create:readme')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)` returns `/create:readme`. Same for `anymore`, `because it is broken`, `until it is fixed`, `today`, `ever again`.\\n- `R1-P1-002` replay: `commandOnlyMentioned('read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does', '/deep:review')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE('review'), prompt)` returns `/deep:review`. Same for `then summarize it`, `then check the changelog`, `then run the test suite`.\\n- Boundary sweep of the allowed trailing words: `yet`, `now`, `for now`, `at all`, `please` all keep the mention reading, which matches the change's stated allowlist. `twice` reads as a request, which is the intended pass-thirteen trade-off.\\n- Boundary sweep of `then`: only `then do a thorough review of this diff` and `then run it` are genuine requests; every other probed `then` clause is read as a request although it asks for something else.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `do not run it today` reads as a request. That is a time limit rather than a refusal, so it is consistent with the change's limit/refusal distinction; it is not counted as part of `R1-P1-001`.\\n- `do not run it twice` reads as a request, the intended behavior. It stays out of the finding.\\n- A refusal ending in `ever again` fails for the same anchor reason as `again`; folded into `R1-P1-001`, not raised separately.\\n- A `then` clause that names the command again (`then run it`) is a request through the pronoun rule as well as the `then` guard; the guard is not what decides it.\\n- No prompt was found in these two rules where a request reads as a mention beyond the intended limits, so the opposite direction stays clean.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The five-word allowlist behaves exactly as written: all five keep a mention.\\n- The two P1 prompts still return the wrong reading on the current tree (working tree matches `e626653ce79`), so neither finding is stale.\\n- The consumer still offers the command for each failing prompt, so both findings have a reachable effect.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Downgrading `R1-P1-001` because `again` can imply a previous run: the probe uses `keeps failing` and `is broken`, where the clause refuses a further run and the prompt contains no request.\\n- Downgrading `R1-P1-002` because `then` often introduces work: five of six probed `then` clauses ask for a read or a different task, so the word alone is not a request marker.\\n- A new finding for `today`: it is a limit, not a refusal, and the change's own comment names limits as requests.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness (consumer cross-reference)\\n- Focus area: `typedCommandForTop`, `attachCommand` and `routeNeedsMode`, plus the generated `MODE_COMMANDS`/`COMMAND_ROWS`/`TRACKED_COMMANDS` consistency for the two commands in the probes.\\n- Reason: the replay confirmed the guard; the next pass asks whether a consumer could still deliver the wrong command through a different path or a table mismatch.\\n- Rotation status: four dimensions covered; consumer cross-reference next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the traceability gate stays closed; expect another recovery or continue decision, not STOP.\\n- Required evidence: consumer return values for a mention and a request prompt, and own-key/table agreement for `/deep:review` and `/create:readme`.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo new finding; both P1s and the P2 remain active and reproduce.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869755792,"end":1794869768916}}}}
