{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869847164,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e69436a8002a8Cnf3v1Y4kyn8","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e6940e0e001zhB07wB0eymGDx","type":"tool","id":"call_61aed748dae64be699949148","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 006 - consumer cross-reference\n\n## Dimension\n\nCorrectness, consumer cross-reference: when the guard withholds or delivers a command, do both consumers behave as the same decision, and do the generated tables agree with the tracked rows for the two commands probed?\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n```text\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\nBINDING: mode=review\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n```\n\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\n\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The pass read only the two scope files and honored the holdout rule.\n\nRecovery note: the iteration-5 stop decision was `STUCK_RECOVERY` (stuckCount 4). This pass follows the recovery strategy's traceability replay by tracing both consumers end to end.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:190-264`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:501-572`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:372-390`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:515-603`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002` remain active.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. `R1-P2-001` remains active.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\nNot re-run; iteration 3's results stand.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc']['sk-create-readme']` is `/create:readme`; `MODE_COMMANDS['system-deep-loop']['review']` is `/deep:review`.\n- `TRACKED_COMMANDS['/create:readme']` is `{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false }`; `TRACKED_COMMANDS['/deep:review']` is `{ policy: 'ask', ownerSkillId: 'system-deep-loop', scorerRow: false }`.\n- Mention prompt through `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), 'read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does')` returns `undefined`; the matching request prompt returns `/create:readme`. The guard decision reaches the offer unchanged.\n- `typedCommandForTop('system-deep-loop', 'run /deep:review now')` returns `{ command: '/deep:review', policy: 'ask', ownerSkillId: 'system-deep-loop' }`; the refused variant returns `undefined`; a top skill that does not own the command returns `undefined`.\n- `routeNeedsMode('system-deep-loop', {action:'defer'}, ['system-deep-loop'])` is `true`; the same call with `action:'route'` is `false`. The mode hint is limited to hubs that have mode commands and to defer/clarify routes.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `commandRowFor('sk-create-readme')` returns `undefined`: the mode id is not a command-row key, and the two tables serve different lookups (mode id → command, skill id → row). The consumer reaches the command through `row.ownerSkillId`, which matches `sk-doc`. No mismatch for the probed commands.\n- The `sameCommandRow` branch in `typedCommandForTop` stayed `false` for every top skill id in the repository's generated tables; the owner check is what delivers both probed commands. This is unchanged by pass fourteen and outside the two rules, so it is recorded as context, not a finding.\n- An unknown deep-loop command (for example `/deep:reviw`) is still not a typed command and is withheld; the diff does not touch that boundary.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Both consumers route the guard's boolean identically: mention → withhold, request → deliver.\n- The generated tables carry both commands once and agree on policy and owner.\n- `routeNeedsMode` still returns false for a route action and for a skill with no mode table.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A consumer finding for the two P1 shapes: the consumer already withholds when the guard returns a mention; the defect is the guard's reading, already carried by the two P1s.\n- A table-mismatch finding: the mode rows and tracked rows agree for both commands.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness (fixture invariance)\n- Focus area: the wrapper matrix, the retired-name loop and the new request rows, to see which invariants the pass-fourteen fixtures join and which they skip.\n- Reason: the consumer path is clean; the remaining surface is the suite's own invariance guarantees, which are the only defense against a future widening.\n- Rotation status: four dimensions plus replay and consumer traces covered.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the traceability gate stays closed; expect recovery again.\n- Required evidence: `PLAIN_ROWS` membership, the wrapper loop at 184-189, and the new rows at 210-218.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo new finding; both P1s and the P2 remain active.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 006 - consumer cross-reference\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nCorrectness, consumer cross-reference: when the guard withholds or delivers a command, do both consumers behave as the same decision, and do the generated tables agree with the tracked rows for the two commands probed?\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n```text\\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\\nBINDING: mode=review\\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\n```\\n\\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\\n\\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The pass read only the two scope files and honored the holdout rule.\\n\\nRecovery note: the iteration-5 stop decision was `STUCK_RECOVERY` (stuckCount 4). This pass follows the recovery strategy's traceability replay by tracing both consumers end to end.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:190-264`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:501-572`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:372-390`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:515-603`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002` remain active.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. `R1-P2-001` remains active.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\nNot re-run; iteration 3's results stand.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc']['sk-create-readme']` is `/create:readme`; `MODE_COMMANDS['system-deep-loop']['review']` is `/deep:review`.\\n- `TRACKED_COMMANDS['/create:readme']` is `{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false }`; `TRACKED_COMMANDS['/deep:review']` is `{ policy: 'ask', ownerSkillId: 'system-deep-loop', scorerRow: false }`.\\n- Mention prompt through `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), 'read the /create:readme document and tell me what it does')` returns `undefined`; the matching request prompt returns `/create:readme`. The guard decision reaches the offer unchanged.\\n- `typedCommandForTop('system-deep-loop', 'run /deep:review now')` returns `{ command: '/deep:review', policy: 'ask', ownerSkillId: 'system-deep-loop' }`; the refused variant returns `undefined`; a top skill that does not own the command returns `undefined`.\\n- `routeNeedsMode('system-deep-loop', {action:'defer'}, ['system-deep-loop'])` is `true`; the same call with `action:'route'` is `false`. The mode hint is limited to hubs that have mode commands and to defer/clarify routes.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `commandRowFor('sk-create-readme')` returns `undefined`: the mode id is not a command-row key, and the two tables serve different lookups (mode id → command, skill id → row). The consumer reaches the command through `row.ownerSkillId`, which matches `sk-doc`. No mismatch for the probed commands.\\n- The `sameCommandRow` branch in `typedCommandForTop` stayed `false` for every top skill id in the repository's generated tables; the owner check is what delivers both probed commands. This is unchanged by pass fourteen and outside the two rules, so it is recorded as context, not a finding.\\n- An unknown deep-loop command (for example `/deep:reviw`) is still not a typed command and is withheld; the diff does not touch that boundary.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Both consumers route the guard's boolean identically: mention → withhold, request → deliver.\\n- The generated tables carry both commands once and agree on policy and owner.\\n- `routeNeedsMode` still returns false for a route action and for a skill with no mode table.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A consumer finding for the two P1 shapes: the consumer already withholds when the guard returns a mention; the defect is the guard's reading, already carried by the two P1s.\\n- A table-mismatch finding: the mode rows and tracked rows agree for both commands.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness (fixture invariance)\\n- Focus area: the wrapper matrix, the retired-name loop and the new request rows, to see which invariants the pass-fourteen fixtures join and which they skip.\\n- Reason: the consumer path is clean; the remaining surface is the suite's own invariance guarantees, which are the only defense against a future widening.\\n- Rotation status: four dimensions plus replay and consumer traces covered.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the traceability gate stays closed; expect recovery again.\\n- Required evidence: `PLAIN_ROWS` membership, the wrapper loop at 184-189, and the new rows at 210-218.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo new finding; both P1s and the P2 remain active.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869835432,"end":1794869847164}}}}
