{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869905319,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e695191b001kX4JPlk6OHEfiM","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e695091f001TxnGbV7I1DwcGo","type":"tool","id":"call_34592626f60f44b18a371714","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 007 - fixture invariance\n\n## Dimension\n\nCorrectness, fixture invariance: which of the suite's own invariants (wrapper matrix, retired-name parity, request/mention tables) the pass-fourteen rows join, and whether the two active boundaries would be caught by a row that does not exist yet.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n```text\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\nBINDING: mode=review\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n```\n\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\n\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The pass read only the two scope files and honored the holdout rule.\n\nRecovery note: the iteration-6 stop decision was `STUCK_RECOVERY` (stuckCount 5). This pass continues line-level fixture analysis.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-73`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:138-229`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:442-482`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002` remain active.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. `R1-P2-001` remains active.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\nNot re-run; iteration 3's results stand.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `PLAIN_ROWS` (`tests:179-182`) is `REFUSE8 + QUESTION2 + REQUEST6 + CONTROL5` plus two or-list rows. The later-refusal rows (`202-208`) and the pass-fourteen request rows (`210-218`) are outside it, so neither the wrapper matrix nor the retired-name loop covers them.\n- Wrapper invariance was re-checked by hand on two new rows (`run /speckit:save and don't run it twice`, `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff`) across backticks, bold, brackets, curly quotes and code tags: every wrapped reading equals the plain reading. The invariant holds; it is simply not asserted for those rows.\n- The two missing mention rows would fail if added: a `REFUSE8`-style row for `/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again` expects `true` and gets `false`, and a mention row for `read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does` expects `true` and gets `false`. Both are reproducible without editing the suite.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `PLAIN_ROWS` membership is not a correctness requirement; it is a coverage choice. The fold runs before every branch, and the hand-check above found no wrapper-dependent difference, so the gap is low-risk and is folded into `R1-P2-001` rather than raised as a second P2.\n- The retired-name loop only substitutes `/create:skill` for whatever command a row names; the new rows have no retired spelling, so excluding them costs nothing for that invariant.\n- The two new request rows that pass through `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` (`open the ... command file, then run it`) are still meaningful rows: they pin the pronoun rule, not the `then` guard.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- All five new request rows assert `false` and pass.\n- The wrapper matrix still covers every row it lists, and the retired-name parity still holds for its own set.\n- Adding the two missing mention rows would fail on the current code, so `R1-P2-001` is a real, test-detectable gap rather than a style preference.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A separate P2 for `PLAIN_ROWS` membership: the hand-check found the invariant already holds, and `R1-P2-001` already asks for the rows that would matter.\n- A finding against the fixture titles: each title matches its assertion for the five new rows.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability (last under the cap)\n- Focus area: re-record both core protocols with their file:line evidence, and confirm the remaining gate state before the cap ends the loop.\n- Reason: the last iteration under `maxIterations` is reserved for the unfinished core protocols; both are `partial` because the two P1s are open, and the cap will stop the loop with them open.\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions and the replay, consumer and fixture traces are covered.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: `dimensionCoverageGate` stays closed by the two `partial` protocols; do not claim a legal STOP.\n- Required evidence: `spec.md:57`, `implementation-summary.md:83`, `acceptance-criteria.md:60`, `tasks.md:131`, and the two code lines.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo new finding; both P1s and the P2 remain active.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-007.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-007.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 007 - fixture invariance\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nCorrectness, fixture invariance: which of the suite's own invariants (wrapper matrix, retired-name parity, request/mention tables) the pass-fourteen rows join, and whether the two active boundaries would be caught by a row that does not exist yet.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n```text\\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\nBINDING: maxIterations=8\\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\\nBINDING: mode=review\\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\n```\\n\\nResolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review; execution=single_review_iteration; state_source=externalized_files.\\n\\nOperator review focus: pass fourteen, area `mention`. The pass read only the two scope files and honored the holdout rule.\\n\\nRecovery note: the iteration-6 stop decision was `STUCK_RECOVERY` (stuckCount 5). This pass continues line-level fixture analysis.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-73`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:138-229`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:442-482`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. `R1-P1-001` and `R1-P1-002` remain active.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. `R1-P2-001` remains active.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\nNot re-run; iteration 3's results stand.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `PLAIN_ROWS` (`tests:179-182`) is `REFUSE8 + QUESTION2 + REQUEST6 + CONTROL5` plus two or-list rows. The later-refusal rows (`202-208`) and the pass-fourteen request rows (`210-218`) are outside it, so neither the wrapper matrix nor the retired-name loop covers them.\\n- Wrapper invariance was re-checked by hand on two new rows (`run /speckit:save and don't run it twice`, `read the /deep:review docs, then do a thorough review of this diff`) across backticks, bold, brackets, curly quotes and code tags: every wrapped reading equals the plain reading. The invariant holds; it is simply not asserted for those rows.\\n- The two missing mention rows would fail if added: a `REFUSE8`-style row for `/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again` expects `true` and gets `false`, and a mention row for `read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does` expects `true` and gets `false`. Both are reproducible without editing the suite.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `PLAIN_ROWS` membership is not a correctness requirement; it is a coverage choice. The fold runs before every branch, and the hand-check above found no wrapper-dependent difference, so the gap is low-risk and is folded into `R1-P2-001` rather than raised as a second P2.\\n- The retired-name loop only substitutes `/create:skill` for whatever command a row names; the new rows have no retired spelling, so excluding them costs nothing for that invariant.\\n- The two new request rows that pass through `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` (`open the ... command file, then run it`) are still meaningful rows: they pin the pronoun rule, not the `then` guard.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- All five new request rows assert `false` and pass.\\n- The wrapper matrix still covers every row it lists, and the retired-name parity still holds for its own set.\\n- Adding the two missing mention rows would fail on the current code, so `R1-P2-001` is a real, test-detectable gap rather than a style preference.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A separate P2 for `PLAIN_ROWS` membership: the hand-check found the invariant already holds, and `R1-P2-001` already asks for the rows that would matter.\\n- A finding against the fixture titles: each title matches its assertion for the five new rows.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability (last under the cap)\\n- Focus area: re-record both core protocols with their file:line evidence, and confirm the remaining gate state before the cap ends the loop.\\n- Reason: the last iteration under `maxIterations` is reserved for the unfinished core protocols; both are `partial` because the two P1s are open, and the cap will stop the loop with them open.\\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions and the replay, consumer and fixture traces are covered.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: `dimensionCoverageGate` stays closed by the two `partial` protocols; do not claim a legal STOP.\\n- Required evidence: `spec.md:57`, `implementation-summary.md:83`, `acceptance-criteria.md:60`, `tasks.md:131`, and the two code lines.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo new finding; both P1s and the P2 remain active.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/iterations/iteration-007.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869893403,"end":1794869905319}}}}
