{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794870129862,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e69828f2001O9z53E2iN7v0ff","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e69818bd001fRNdauHNY8x6zW","type":"tool","id":"call_742c7a5b2bef4f078b7cbd01","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - command surfacing pass fourteen (mention area)\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Area: `mention` (pass fourteen)\n- Lineage: `review/lineages/mention-14`\n- Session: `fanout-mention-14-1794868189353-tsxtos`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Iterations: 8 of 8\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (terminal gate `coverage` still failing at the stop)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL**\n- **hasAdvisories: false** (the verdict is not PASS; the P2 is listed as an advisory below)\n- **Counts the verdict used:** P0 = 0, P1 = 2, P2 = 1\n- **Self-check outcomes:** `R1-P1-001` confirmed P1; `R1-P1-002` confirmed P1; `R1-P2-001` confirmed P2. No finding was downgraded or called a false positive, so the counts are unchanged.\n- **Review scope summary:** both pass-fourteen `mention` scope files, read in full at `e626653ce79`; the diff from `932aff4e437`; phase-040 records consulted for traceability only. Every configured dimension (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) was covered, and both files were read under all four.\n- **Operator review focus:** Review pass fourteen. First read `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-14.txt` and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\n\nBoth P1s are regressions introduced by the pass-thirteen fixes to the two rules this area owns. Neither is a security defect; the security pass found no injection, backtracking, or fold-based bypass. The traceability gate is closed because the phase-040 records and AC-005 cannot be satisfied while the two P1s are open.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required: the verdict is CONDITIONAL with two active P1 findings.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-P1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"A refusal whose object carries a reason or a repeat adverb is read as a request\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:415\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-P1-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"A document naming followed by any then clause is read as a request\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-P2-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The new fixtures pin neither boundary the two rules changed\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:210\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"finding\": \"R1-P1-001\",\n      \"action\": \"Make the clause-end refusal read complete when the refusal predicate ends the clause, not when the pronoun does, while keeping `don't run it twice` and `never run it without a budget` as requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"finding\": \"R1-P1-002\",\n      \"action\": \"Keep a document naming a mention unless the `then` clause itself asks to run the named command or to do the command's work; a read-only or unrelated `then` clause must not turn it into a request.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-3\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"finding\": \"R1-P2-001\",\n      \"action\": \"Add failing-first mention rows for both boundary shapes before the rule edits.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Record that a post-name refusal is complete when the refusal clause ends, including when the predicate carries a reason or a repeat adverb such as `again`, `anymore`, `because ...` or `until ...`.\",\n    \"Record that a command named as a document (with `the`, `this` or `that`) stays a mention when the following `then` clause asks only for a read or for unrelated work.\",\n    \"Carry the two P1s and the P2 forward into the phase that owns pass fourteen's remediation.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add the two failing-first rows (`/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again` and `read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does`) and confirm they fail before any rule edit.\",\n    \"Change `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` so the clause-end test is on the refusal, not on `it`, and keep the two recorded request rows green.\",\n    \"Replace the blanket `then` test in the document branch with a work-request test that leaves `then tell me`, `then summarize` and `then run the test suite` as mentions.\",\n    \"Re-run the guard suite and the wrapper matrix; no other row may move.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": {\n    \"R1-P1-001\": \"correctness-regression\",\n    \"R1-P1-002\": \"rule-precedence\",\n    \"R1-P2-001\": \"test-coverage-gap\"\n  },\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:415\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:533\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:259\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:210-218\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### R1-P1-001 - A refusal whose object carries a reason is read as a request (P1, correctness)\n\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:415`\n- **Evidence:** `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` now requires `it` at the clause end and allows only `yet`, `now`, `for now`, `at all` and `please` after it. `commandOnlyMentioned('/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again', '/create:readme')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)` returns `/create:readme` (policy `start`, mutating).\n- **Impact:** a reader who refuses the command is offered it, and a `start` command can begin work the reader ruled out. The code contradicts its own comment at 412-414 (\"the refusal has to end its clause\").\n- **Fix recommendation:** anchor the clause end on the refusal predicate rather than on the pronoun, and keep limit clauses (`twice`, `without a budget`) as requests.\n- **Disposition:** active\n- **Finding class:** correctness-regression\n- **Scope proof:** direct execution of the exported guard and consumer on five prompts; the removed pattern ended at `it\\b`, so the same inputs read as mentions before this branch.\n- **Affected surface hints:** `commandOnlyMentioned:463`, `typedCommandForTop:259`, `attachCommand:533`, the later-refusal fixtures.\n\n### R1-P1-002 - A document naming followed by any `then` clause is read as a request (P1, correctness)\n\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465`\n- **Evidence:** `!/\\bthen\\b/.test(clause)` suppresses the document reading whenever `then` appears after the name. `commandOnlyMentioned('read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does', '/deep:review')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE('review'), prompt)` returns `/deep:review`. The same holds for `then summarize it`, `then check the changelog` and `then run the test suite`.\n- **Impact:** a reader who only reads about the command is offered a costly multi-pass command. The deep-loop depth gate at 549-552 does not withhold it because `typedCommandIn` finds the typed name.\n- **Fix recommendation:** keep the document reading unless the `then` clause itself names a run of the command or the command's work; a read-only follow-up is not a request.\n- **Disposition:** active\n- **Finding class:** rule-precedence\n- **Scope proof:** direct execution on six `then` clauses; `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` already carries `, then run it`, so the guard only changes read-only follow-ups.\n- **Affected surface hints:** `attachCommand:533`, `attachCommand:549-552`, `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT:423`, document fixtures at tests 221-226.\n\n### R1-P2-001 - The new fixtures pin neither boundary the two rules changed (P2, correctness)\n\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:210`\n- **Evidence:** the five new request rows cover a limit after `it` and a work clause after `then`; no row covers a refusal with a trailing reason and no row covers a `then` read-only follow-up. Adding either row to a mention table fails today.\n- **Impact:** the suite stays green if either boundary is widened or narrowed again.\n- **Fix recommendation:** add the two failing-first rows before the rule edits.\n- **Disposition:** active (advisory)\n- **Finding class:** test-coverage-gap\n- **Scope proof:** read the fixture tables at 202-218 and 221-229; the only `then` row asserts a request and the only post-name refusals end at `it`.\n- **Affected surface hints:** request table 210-218, `REFUSE8` 42-51, document table 221-226.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **WS-1 (P1, R1-P1-001):** add the failing-first rows, then change the clause-end anchor so a refusal ending its clause is honored even when the predicate carries a reason. Keep `twice` and `without a budget` as requests.\n2. **WS-2 (P1, R1-P1-002):** replace the blanket `then` test with a work-request test; `then tell me`, `then summarize`, `then check` and `then run the test suite` must stay mentions, while `then run it` and `then do a thorough review` stay requests.\n3. **WS-3 (P2, R1-P2-001):** add both failing-first fixture rows and keep the wrapper/retired-name invariants intact for them.\n4. **Verification for all three:** the guard suite green, the two recorded request rows (`don't run it twice`, `never run it without a budget`) unchanged, and the wrapper matrix unchanged.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- A refusal after the name is complete when the refusal clause ends, whatever reason or repeat adverb follows the predicate; a limit on how a requested run may happen is not a refusal.\n- A command named as a document with a determiner stays a mention when a following `then` clause asks only for a read or for unrelated work; only a clause that asks to run the command or do its work makes it a request.\n- The two pass-thirteen fixes each carry one boundary case that the original fixtures did not pin; the follow-on phase adds those rows before the rule edits.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- T1: add `['/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again', '/create:readme']` to the mention table and `['read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does', '/deep:review']` to the document table; confirm both fail on the current head.\n- T2: adjust `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` (line 415) so the end anchor is on the refusal predicate; keep the `twice`/`without a budget` rows green.\n- T3: adjust the document branch (line 465) so `then` alone does not suppress the mention; keep `then run it` and `then do a thorough review` as requests.\n- T4: run the guard suite and the wrapper matrix; record the before/after counts. No other file changes.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\n|----------|--------|----------|------------------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md:57`, `040-final-alignment-loop/implementation-summary.md:83`, `command-attach.ts:415`, `command-attach.ts:465` | The document-naming shape with a `then` read-only follow-up is offered (R1-P1-002); the refusal rule requires the pronoun to end the clause (R1-P1-001). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `040-final-alignment-loop/acceptance-criteria.md:60`, `040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:131` | AC-005 is `Unmet` for pass 14 (two P1 open); CHK-FIX-002 does not cover the two new boundary shapes. |\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\nAll four overlay protocols are `notApplicable`: the diff contains no skill definition, no agent mirror, no feature-catalog row and no playbook capability.\n\n### AC Coverage\n\n`exempt`: the target folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md` at its root; the phase children own their acceptance criteria, and the phase-040 rows are reported under `checklist_evidence` instead.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- The `PLAIN_ROWS` membership gap for the newest fixtures (wrapper matrix and retired-name loop do not include them) is folded into R1-P2-001; a hand-check found wrapper invariance already holds.\n- A second P2 for the code comments at 412-414 and 420-422 was not raised: both comments state the intent the two P1s say the code fails, so fixing either rule fixes its comment.\n- The dead-looking `sameCommandRow` branch in `typedCommandForTop` is pre-existing and outside the two changed rules; recorded as context only.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\nThe loop recorded seven `STUCK_RECOVERY` decisions (iterations 2-7) and a final `maxIterationsReached`; the recovery path changed granularity from file to line and replayed the two protocols, but no pivot transaction was opened, so the divergence maps are empty.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- `searchCoverage` (latest record): required `[]`, covered `[]`, ruledOut `[]`, deferred `[]`, blocked `[]`, graphCoverageMode `graph`.\n- `candidateCoverage`: covered `clause_boundary`, `rule_precedence`, `test_boundary_pinning`; ruledOut `backtracking_dos`, `command_name_escaping`, `markup_fold_consent`, `regex_injection`, `typed_command_boundary`.\n- `searchDebt`: `[]` (no deferred or blocked bug class).\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: the five ruled-out classes above, each with the action and evidence recorded in iterations 1-2.\n- `cleanSearchProof`: the static/escaped pattern construction, the timing probe, the wrapper-fold check and the typed-command boundary check.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence Summary\n\n| Iteration | Focus | New findings (P0/P1/P2) | Ratio | Stop decision |\n|-----------|-------|--------------------------|-------|---------------|\n| 1 | correctness | 0/2/1 | 1.00 | CONTINUE |\n| 2 | security | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | CONTINUE |\n| 3 | traceability | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\n| 4 | maintainability | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\n| 5 | correctness replay | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\n| 6 | consumer cross-reference | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\n| 7 | fixture invariance | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\n| 8 | traceability (cap) | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STOP `maxIterationsReached` |\n\n### Coverage Summary\n\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability - all covered.\n- Files: `command-attach.ts` and `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` - both reviewed under all four dimensions.\n- Terminal gates at the stop: evidence `pass`, scope `pass`, coverage `fail` (`traceability-incomplete`).\n- Active findings: 3 (2 P1, 1 P2); resolved: 0.\n\n### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- Regex injection: every built pattern is static or `escapePhrase`d.\n- Backtracking DoS: 400k-character adversarial prompts complete in 11 ms or less.\n- Markup fold bypass: wrapped refusals still read as refusals.\n- Typed-command boundary: a doc path, extension or longer name is still rejected.\n- A request-reads-as-a-mention defect in the two changed rules beyond the intended limits: none found.\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (whole file, `e626653ce79`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (whole file)\n- `review/review-brief-14.txt`, `review/review-scope-14.txt`\n- `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md`, `implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `tasks.md`\n- `sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`\n\nHoldout rule honored: no `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` was opened; no forbidden diff was run; no score summary or CLI session text was read.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report - command surfacing pass fourteen (mention area)\\n\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Area: `mention` (pass fourteen)\\n- Lineage: `review/lineages/mention-14`\\n- Session: `fanout-mention-14-1794868189353-tsxtos`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Iterations: 8 of 8\\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (terminal gate `coverage` still failing at the stop)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL**\\n- **hasAdvisories: false** (the verdict is not PASS; the P2 is listed as an advisory below)\\n- **Counts the verdict used:** P0 = 0, P1 = 2, P2 = 1\\n- **Self-check outcomes:** `R1-P1-001` confirmed P1; `R1-P1-002` confirmed P1; `R1-P2-001` confirmed P2. No finding was downgraded or called a false positive, so the counts are unchanged.\\n- **Review scope summary:** both pass-fourteen `mention` scope files, read in full at `e626653ce79`; the diff from `932aff4e437`; phase-040 records consulted for traceability only. Every configured dimension (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) was covered, and both files were read under all four.\\n- **Operator review focus:** Review pass fourteen. First read `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-14.txt` and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\\n\\nBoth P1s are regressions introduced by the pass-thirteen fixes to the two rules this area owns. Neither is a security defect; the security pass found no injection, backtracking, or fold-based bypass. The traceability gate is closed because the phase-040 records and AC-005 cannot be satisfied while the two P1s are open.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required: the verdict is CONDITIONAL with two active P1 findings.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-P1-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"A refusal whose object carries a reason or a repeat adverb is read as a request\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:415\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-P1-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"A document naming followed by any then clause is read as a request\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-P2-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The new fixtures pin neither boundary the two rules changed\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:210\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"finding\\\": \\\"R1-P1-001\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Make the clause-end refusal read complete when the refusal predicate ends the clause, not when the pronoun does, while keeping `don't run it twice` and `never run it without a budget` as requests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"finding\\\": \\\"R1-P1-002\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Keep a document naming a mention unless the `then` clause itself asks to run the named command or to do the command's work; a read-only or unrelated `then` clause must not turn it into a request.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"finding\\\": \\\"R1-P2-001\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Add failing-first mention rows for both boundary shapes before the rule edits.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Record that a post-name refusal is complete when the refusal clause ends, including when the predicate carries a reason or a repeat adverb such as `again`, `anymore`, `because ...` or `until ...`.\\\",\\n    \\\"Record that a command named as a document (with `the`, `this` or `that`) stays a mention when the following `then` clause asks only for a read or for unrelated work.\\\",\\n    \\\"Carry the two P1s and the P2 forward into the phase that owns pass fourteen's remediation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add the two failing-first rows (`/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again` and `read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does`) and confirm they fail before any rule edit.\\\",\\n    \\\"Change `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` so the clause-end test is on the refusal, not on `it`, and keep the two recorded request rows green.\\\",\\n    \\\"Replace the blanket `then` test in the document branch with a work-request test that leaves `then tell me`, `then summarize` and `then run the test suite` as mentions.\\\",\\n    \\\"Re-run the guard suite and the wrapper matrix; no other row may move.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": {\\n    \\\"R1-P1-001\\\": \\\"correctness-regression\\\",\\n    \\\"R1-P1-002\\\": \\\"rule-precedence\\\",\\n    \\\"R1-P2-001\\\": \\\"test-coverage-gap\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:415\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:533\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:259\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:210-218\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### R1-P1-001 - A refusal whose object carries a reason is read as a request (P1, correctness)\\n\\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:415`\\n- **Evidence:** `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` now requires `it` at the clause end and allows only `yet`, `now`, `for now`, `at all` and `please` after it. `commandOnlyMentioned('/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again', '/create:readme')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)` returns `/create:readme` (policy `start`, mutating).\\n- **Impact:** a reader who refuses the command is offered it, and a `start` command can begin work the reader ruled out. The code contradicts its own comment at 412-414 (\\\"the refusal has to end its clause\\\").\\n- **Fix recommendation:** anchor the clause end on the refusal predicate rather than on the pronoun, and keep limit clauses (`twice`, `without a budget`) as requests.\\n- **Disposition:** active\\n- **Finding class:** correctness-regression\\n- **Scope proof:** direct execution of the exported guard and consumer on five prompts; the removed pattern ended at `it\\\\b`, so the same inputs read as mentions before this branch.\\n- **Affected surface hints:** `commandOnlyMentioned:463`, `typedCommandForTop:259`, `attachCommand:533`, the later-refusal fixtures.\\n\\n### R1-P1-002 - A document naming followed by any `then` clause is read as a request (P1, correctness)\\n\\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:465`\\n- **Evidence:** `!/\\\\bthen\\\\b/.test(clause)` suppresses the document reading whenever `then` appears after the name. `commandOnlyMentioned('read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does', '/deep:review')` returns `false`; `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE('review'), prompt)` returns `/deep:review`. The same holds for `then summarize it`, `then check the changelog` and `then run the test suite`.\\n- **Impact:** a reader who only reads about the command is offered a costly multi-pass command. The deep-loop depth gate at 549-552 does not withhold it because `typedCommandIn` finds the typed name.\\n- **Fix recommendation:** keep the document reading unless the `then` clause itself names a run of the command or the command's work; a read-only follow-up is not a request.\\n- **Disposition:** active\\n- **Finding class:** rule-precedence\\n- **Scope proof:** direct execution on six `then` clauses; `COMMAND_ASKED_BY_PRONOUN` already carries `, then run it`, so the guard only changes read-only follow-ups.\\n- **Affected surface hints:** `attachCommand:533`, `attachCommand:549-552`, `COMMAND_AS_DOCUMENT:423`, document fixtures at tests 221-226.\\n\\n### R1-P2-001 - The new fixtures pin neither boundary the two rules changed (P2, correctness)\\n\\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:210`\\n- **Evidence:** the five new request rows cover a limit after `it` and a work clause after `then`; no row covers a refusal with a trailing reason and no row covers a `then` read-only follow-up. Adding either row to a mention table fails today.\\n- **Impact:** the suite stays green if either boundary is widened or narrowed again.\\n- **Fix recommendation:** add the two failing-first rows before the rule edits.\\n- **Disposition:** active (advisory)\\n- **Finding class:** test-coverage-gap\\n- **Scope proof:** read the fixture tables at 202-218 and 221-229; the only `then` row asserts a request and the only post-name refusals end at `it`.\\n- **Affected surface hints:** request table 210-218, `REFUSE8` 42-51, document table 221-226.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **WS-1 (P1, R1-P1-001):** add the failing-first rows, then change the clause-end anchor so a refusal ending its clause is honored even when the predicate carries a reason. Keep `twice` and `without a budget` as requests.\\n2. **WS-2 (P1, R1-P1-002):** replace the blanket `then` test with a work-request test; `then tell me`, `then summarize`, `then check` and `then run the test suite` must stay mentions, while `then run it` and `then do a thorough review` stay requests.\\n3. **WS-3 (P2, R1-P2-001):** add both failing-first fixture rows and keep the wrapper/retired-name invariants intact for them.\\n4. **Verification for all three:** the guard suite green, the two recorded request rows (`don't run it twice`, `never run it without a budget`) unchanged, and the wrapper matrix unchanged.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- A refusal after the name is complete when the refusal clause ends, whatever reason or repeat adverb follows the predicate; a limit on how a requested run may happen is not a refusal.\\n- A command named as a document with a determiner stays a mention when a following `then` clause asks only for a read or for unrelated work; only a clause that asks to run the command or do its work makes it a request.\\n- The two pass-thirteen fixes each carry one boundary case that the original fixtures did not pin; the follow-on phase adds those rows before the rule edits.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- T1: add `['/create:readme keeps failing, never run it again', '/create:readme']` to the mention table and `['read the /deep:review docs, then tell me what it does', '/deep:review']` to the document table; confirm both fail on the current head.\\n- T2: adjust `COMMAND_DECLINED_BY_PRONOUN` (line 415) so the end anchor is on the refusal predicate; keep the `twice`/`without a budget` rows green.\\n- T3: adjust the document branch (line 465) so `then` alone does not suppress the mention; keep `then run it` and `then do a thorough review` as requests.\\n- T4: run the guard suite and the wrapper matrix; record the before/after counts. No other file changes.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\\n|----------|--------|----------|------------------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md:57`, `040-final-alignment-loop/implementation-summary.md:83`, `command-attach.ts:415`, `command-attach.ts:465` | The document-naming shape with a `then` read-only follow-up is offered (R1-P1-002); the refusal rule requires the pronoun to end the clause (R1-P1-001). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `040-final-alignment-loop/acceptance-criteria.md:60`, `040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:131` | AC-005 is `Unmet` for pass 14 (two P1 open); CHK-FIX-002 does not cover the two new boundary shapes. |\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\nAll four overlay protocols are `notApplicable`: the diff contains no skill definition, no agent mirror, no feature-catalog row and no playbook capability.\\n\\n### AC Coverage\\n\\n`exempt`: the target folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md` at its root; the phase children own their acceptance criteria, and the phase-040 rows are reported under `checklist_evidence` instead.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- The `PLAIN_ROWS` membership gap for the newest fixtures (wrapper matrix and retired-name loop do not include them) is folded into R1-P2-001; a hand-check found wrapper invariance already holds.\\n- A second P2 for the code comments at 412-414 and 420-422 was not raised: both comments state the intent the two P1s say the code fails, so fixing either rule fixes its comment.\\n- The dead-looking `sameCommandRow` branch in `typedCommandForTop` is pre-existing and outside the two changed rules; recorded as context only.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\nThe loop recorded seven `STUCK_RECOVERY` decisions (iterations 2-7) and a final `maxIterationsReached`; the recovery path changed granularity from file to line and replayed the two protocols, but no pivot transaction was opened, so the divergence maps are empty.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- `searchCoverage` (latest record): required `[]`, covered `[]`, ruledOut `[]`, deferred `[]`, blocked `[]`, graphCoverageMode `graph`.\\n- `candidateCoverage`: covered `clause_boundary`, `rule_precedence`, `test_boundary_pinning`; ruledOut `backtracking_dos`, `command_name_escaping`, `markup_fold_consent`, `regex_injection`, `typed_command_boundary`.\\n- `searchDebt`: `[]` (no deferred or blocked bug class).\\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: the five ruled-out classes above, each with the action and evidence recorded in iterations 1-2.\\n- `cleanSearchProof`: the static/escaped pattern construction, the timing probe, the wrapper-fold check and the typed-command boundary check.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence Summary\\n\\n| Iteration | Focus | New findings (P0/P1/P2) | Ratio | Stop decision |\\n|-----------|-------|--------------------------|-------|---------------|\\n| 1 | correctness | 0/2/1 | 1.00 | CONTINUE |\\n| 2 | security | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | CONTINUE |\\n| 3 | traceability | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\\n| 4 | maintainability | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\\n| 5 | correctness replay | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\\n| 6 | consumer cross-reference | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\\n| 7 | fixture invariance | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STUCK_RECOVERY |\\n| 8 | traceability (cap) | 0/0/0 | 0.00 | STOP `maxIterationsReached` |\\n\\n### Coverage Summary\\n\\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability - all covered.\\n- Files: `command-attach.ts` and `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` - both reviewed under all four dimensions.\\n- Terminal gates at the stop: evidence `pass`, scope `pass`, coverage `fail` (`traceability-incomplete`).\\n- Active findings: 3 (2 P1, 1 P2); resolved: 0.\\n\\n### Ruled-Out Claims\\n\\n- Regex injection: every built pattern is static or `escapePhrase`d.\\n- Backtracking DoS: 400k-character adversarial prompts complete in 11 ms or less.\\n- Markup fold bypass: wrapped refusals still read as refusals.\\n- Typed-command boundary: a doc path, extension or longer name is still rejected.\\n- A request-reads-as-a-mention defect in the two changed rules beyond the intended limits: none found.\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (whole file, `e626653ce79`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (whole file)\\n- `review/review-brief-14.txt`, `review/review-scope-14.txt`\\n- `040-final-alignment-loop/spec.md`, `implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `tasks.md`\\n- `sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`\\n\\nHoldout rule honored: no `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` was opened; no forbidden diff was run; no score summary or CLI session text was read.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794870094066,"end":1794870129862}}}}
