{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794870311056,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e69b6bea001VaKwwAt8lmX4Rm","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae6ffeaD8lGAJ4oqvNMo","messageID":"msg_1e69b5a9f001MJYOklBYa6bFeU","type":"tool","id":"call_8dc0d8488a5d4dba90514c46","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- Regex injection: every built pattern is static or `escapePhrase`d.\n- Backtracking DoS: 400k-character adversarial prompts complete in 11 ms or less.\n- Markup fold bypass: wrapped refusals still read as refusals.\n- Typed-command boundary: a doc path, extension or longer name is still rejected.\n- A request-reads-as-a-mention defect in the two changed rules beyond the intended limits: none found.\n\n### Verdict Correction\n\n`review-verdict.cjs` first ran before the terminal-gates row existed and returned `CONDITIONAL` (no failed gate was visible). After `terminal-gates.cjs` recorded `coverage: fail`, the same script returned `FAIL` with `failed_required_gate_ids: [\"coverage\"]`. The report, the dashboard and the final `synthesis_complete` row carry `FAIL`; the earlier `synthesis_complete` row (sequence 19) is superseded by the corrected row (sequence 20) and is kept only as ledger history. No finding count changed.","oldString":"### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- Regex injection: every built pattern is static or `escapePhrase`d.\n- Backtracking DoS: 400k-character adversarial prompts complete in 11 ms or less.\n- Markup fold bypass: wrapped refusals still read as refusals.\n- Typed-command boundary: a doc path, extension or longer name is still rejected.\n- A request-reads-as-a-mention defect in the two changed rules beyond the intended limits: none found.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md\n@@ -226,8 +226,12 @@\n - Markup fold bypass: wrapped refusals still read as refusals.\n - Typed-command boundary: a doc path, extension or longer name is still rejected.\n - A request-reads-as-a-mention defect in the two changed rules beyond the intended limits: none found.\n \n+### Verdict Correction\n+\n+`review-verdict.cjs` first ran before the terminal-gates row existed and returned `CONDITIONAL` (no failed gate was visible). After `terminal-gates.cjs` recorded `coverage: fail`, the same script returned `FAIL` with `failed_required_gate_ids: [\"coverage\"]`. The report, the dashboard and the final `synthesis_complete` row carry `FAIL`; the earlier `synthesis_complete` row (sequence 19) is superseded by the corrected row (sequence 20) and is kept only as ledger history. No finding count changed.\n+\n ### Sources Reviewed\n \n - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (whole file, `e626653ce79`)\n - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (whole file)\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-14/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResul